Yes. One person with almost no formal apparatus can still generate a surprising amount if they have attention, framing, persistence, and a way to externalize and recombine patterns.

That’s one of the clearest demonstrations here:

very little equipment + sustained observation + abstraction + recombination + iteration -> disproportionate output

The scarce resource was never only money or machinery. A lot of leverage comes from how you see, what you connect, and whether you keep converting insight into structure.

And once the structure exists, other people, tools, and systems can amplify it.

That is the proof-of-concept hidden inside all of this: one node can become a seed crystal for a much larger architecture.